IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-16.l4 -- ARTICLE 16 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT TO RECTIFICATION (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 222-224 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the Section 3 heading at
-- 220-221 and the two heading lines of Article 16 at 222-223 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN for a right, a DEONTIC for the regulative rule.
-- WHOSE.  The data subject's CLAIM against the controller; the controller's duty is its correlative.  Article 11(2): see
-- P2-art-15.l4 (each function takes P1's answer `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied`).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 16 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 16 rectify the inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject without undue delay`
    `Art 16 complete the incomplete personal data concerning the data subject`

§ `Article 16: rectification and completion`

-- src:224 | The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller without undue delay the rectification of inaccurate personal data concerning him or her.
@ref Art 16 first sentence (src:224)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data concerning the data subject are inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16 the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the rectification of inaccurate personal data concerning him or her` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF `the personal data concerning the data subject are inaccurate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rectification of inaccurate personal data": accurate data are outside the grant, and the text does not say no to them in its own words
    -- "without undue delay": the time within which the controller must act; no number is stated, so no deadline is encoded (NOTES, Rules with no breach path).

-- src:224 | Taking into account the purposes of the processing, the data subject shall have the right to have incomplete personal data completed, including by means of providing a supplementary statement.
@ref Art 16 second sentence (src:224)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data concerning the data subject are incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `completion is called for, taking into account the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject provides a supplementary statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16 the data subject has the right to have incomplete personal data completed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the data subject shall have the right": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF `the personal data concerning the data subject are incomplete` AND `completion is called for, taking into account the purposes of the processing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Taking into account the purposes of the processing, the data subject shall have the right to have incomplete personal data completed": data that are complete, or whose completion the purposes do not call for, are outside the grant
    -- "including by means of providing a supplementary statement": one way of completing; `the data subject provides a supplementary statement` is not read (a list that includes).

GIVEN `the personal data concerning the data subject are inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 16 action`
`Art 16 the controller must rectify the inaccurate personal data without undue delay` MEANS
    IF `the personal data concerning the data subject are inaccurate` AND NOT (`Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 16 rectify the inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject without undue delay`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- "without undue delay" is not a number, so no WITHIN is written and no deadline is invented: the rule can stand or be fulfilled and never be breached (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

-- src:224 | Taking into account the purposes of the processing, the data subject shall have the right to have incomplete personal data completed, including by means of providing a supplementary statement.
@ref Art 16 second sentence: the controller's duty to complete (src:224)
GIVEN `Art 16 the data subject has the right to have incomplete personal data completed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 16 action`
`Art 16 the controller must complete the incomplete personal data` MEANS
    IF `Art 16 the data subject has the right to have incomplete personal data completed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 16 complete the incomplete personal data concerning the data subject`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the text names the controller ("from the controller" in the first sentence, which this sentence continues) and the act (completing); no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path); the rule takes the answer of the right, as `Art 20(1) the controller shall not hinder ...` does (R8)
